{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked a cobbler orchestrator \"stitch\" task (#5561) for generation-run44 of the go-unix-utils project. This is an automated code generation pipeline where a \"measure\" phase proposes work and a \"stitch\" phase executes it. The task prompt provides full project context including all SRDs, architecture, source code, and coding standards. The intent is to implement Go code for specific requirements that were selected by the measure phase. However, before implementation could begin, the user sent a critical instruction to provide a text-only summary instead of continuing with tool calls.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Cobbler orchestrator pipeline: measure (proposes tasks) → stitch (implements code)\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils verified via differential testing\n   - pkg/testutils provides RunDiffTests harness comparing Go binary vs GNU reference binary\n   - pkg/sys provides syscall abstractions (Stat, Lstat, TerminalWidth, InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n   - pkg/format provides output formatting (HumanSize, FileTypeColor, PadRight/PadLeft, Columns)\n   - pkg/hashutil provides shared hash formatting and verification\n   - pkg/sizeparse parses human-readable size strings\n   - pkg/encutil provides encoding/decoding for base32/base64/basenc\n   - All cmd/ utilities must call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main\n   - Differential tests use exec.LookPath + t.Skip for graceful handling of missing reference binaries\n   - LC_ALL=C is set by default in all differential tests\n   - Branch: task/generation-run44-5561\n   - Git is managed externally - NO git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `.cobbler/history/2026-05-23-22-25-21-measure-stats.yaml`\n     - Read to understand measure phase output\n     - Shows task_id 5561, status success, 0 diff (measure proposes work but doesn't write code)\n     - LOC: production 25074, test 22195\n   - `.cobbler/history/2026-05-23-22-25-21-measure-prompt.yaml`\n     - Partially read (first 100 lines only) - this is the INPUT to measure, not the output\n     - Only saw the beginning of project context, not the actual task proposal\n   - All pkg/ source code is provided inline in the prompt (pkg/sys, pkg/format, pkg/testutils, pkg/hashutil, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/encutil)\n   - requirement_states shows SRDs with \"ready\" requirements: srd004-ts, srd095-nohup through srd114-vidir\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was still in the investigation phase\n   - Did not get far enough to identify what specific requirements to implement\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Was attempting to determine which specific requirements the measure phase selected for this stitch task\n   - The measure-stats.yaml showed 0 diff which is expected (measure proposes, doesn't implement)\n   - The measure-prompt.yaml reading only got the first 100 lines which was project context, not the task assignment\n   - Would need to read the measure-log.log file to see what the measure phase actually proposed as the task\n   - Alternatively, the stitch-prompt would contain the full task description if a stitch was subsequently triggered\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive orchestrator task prompt containing the full stitch task definition for #5561, including all project context, SRDs, source code, execution constitution, coding standards, requirement states, package contracts, and constraints. The task section says to review context, plan approach, implement, and verify.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - instructs to provide analysis and summary blocks only, no tool usage.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Determine which specific SRD requirements this stitch task should implement (need to read measure-log.log or the stitch orchestrator log)\n   - Implement the code for those requirements following the execution constitution\n   - Verify compilation with `go build` and tests with `go test`\n   - Ensure all acceptance criteria are met\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was in the very early investigation phase of the stitch task. I had just read the measure stats file (confirming the measure completed successfully) and begun reading the measure prompt file (only got 100 lines of preamble). I had NOT yet identified what specific code to write because I hadn't found the actual task assignment from the measure phase. The measure-log.log file (`.cobbler/history/2026-05-23-22-25-21-measure-log.log`) would contain the measure's proposed task description, which is what the stitch agent needs to implement.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read `.cobbler/history/2026-05-23-22-25-21-measure-log.log` to find the specific task proposal from the measure phase - this will tell us which SRD requirements to implement and which files to create/modify. Without this information, implementation cannot proceed. The task prompt says: \"Follow these steps in order. Complete each step before moving to the next. 1. Review provided context... 2. Plan approach — Before writing code, determine: What exists already...\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5561/7bf3d195-37dc-4716-b8df-76f355abf711.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":nu