{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V4MDuvmMmYXRTCk93fAF7J","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd093-mknod\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/mknod: Make Block or Character Special Files\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships mknod but the GNU version supports --mode (-m) for setting permissions.\n6\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gmknod, installed\n7\t  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential\n8\t  testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Create block special, character special, or FIFO special files.\n12\t  - G2: Support permission mode specification at creation.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gmknod via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Special file creation\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: \"Must accept NAME TYPE [MAJOR MINOR] arguments. TYPE is b (block special), c or u (character special), or p (FIFO). Block and character types require MAJOR and MINOR device numbers.\"\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"-m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the file's permission bits to MODE (octal or symbolic). Default is 0666 modified by umask for FIFOs, 0660 for device files.\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: Must exit 1 with an error when arguments are invalid (wrong count, non-numeric device numbers, FIFO with device numbers given).\n25\t\n26\t  R2:\n27\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n28\t    items:\n29\t      - R2.1:\n30\t          text: Must exit 0 when the special file is created successfully.\n31\t      - R2.2:\n32\t          text: Must exit 1 when creation fails or arguments are invalid.\n33\t      - R2.3:\n34\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n35\t\n36\tnon_goals:\n37\t  - cmd/mknod does not implement SELinux context setting.\n38\t\n39\tacceptance_criteria:\n40\t  - id: AC1\n41\t    criterion: \"mknod pipe1 p creates a FIFO, matching gmknod.\"\n42\t    traces:\n43\t      - R1.1\n44\t  - id: AC2\n45\t    criterion: \"mknod -m 644 pipe1 p creates a FIFO with mode 644, matching gmknod.\"\n46\t    traces:\n47\t      - R1.2\n48\t  - id: AC3\n49\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gmknod passes for all required test cases.\"\n50\t    traces:\n51\t      - R1.1\n52\t      - R1.2\n53\t      - R1.3\n54\t  - id: AC4\n55\t    criterion: \"cmd/mknod compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R1.1\n58\t      - R1.2\n59\t      - R1.3\n60\t      - R2.1\n61\t      - R2.2\n62\t      - R2.3\n63\t\n64\tpackage_contract:\n65\t  imports:\n66\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bf3d195-37dc-4716-b8df-76f355abf711","uuid":"a4d4557f-571b-4eeb-9ed9-08213a1667d5","timestamp":"2026-05-24T02:31:12.840Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5561/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd093-mknod.yaml","content":"id: srd093-mknod\ntitle: \"cmd/mknod: Make Block or Character Special Files\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships mknod but the GNU version supports --mode (-m) for setting permissions.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gmknod, installed\n  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential\n  testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Create block special, character special, or FIFO special files.\n  - G2: Support permission mode specification at creation.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gmknod via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Special file creation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"Must accept NAME TYPE [MAJOR MINOR] arguments. TYPE is b (block special), c or u (character special), or p (FIFO). Block and character types require MAJOR and MINOR device numbers.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the file's permission bits to MODE (octal or symbolic). Default is 0666 modified by umask for FIFOs, 0660 for device files.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 with an error when arguments are invalid (wrong count, non-numeric device numbers, FIFO with device numbers given).\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when the special file is created successfully.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when creation fails or arguments are invalid.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/mknod does not implement SELinux context setting.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"mknod pipe1 p creates a FIFO, matching gmknod.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"mknod -m 644 pipe1 p creates a FIFO with mode 644, matching gmknod.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gmknod passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/mknod compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
