{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EFurRFHCynfWf24vLJGSRD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good progress! Only 2 failures left: invalid major/minor device numbers. The issue is that GNU doesn't print \"Try 'mknod --help' for more information.\" after device number errors. I need to differentiate between errors that include the \"Try\" hint and errors that don't.\n\nLooking at the pattern:\n- \"missing operand\" → includes \"Try...\"\n- \"missing operand after...\" → includes \"Try...\"\n- \"extra operand...\" → includes \"Try...\"\n- \"invalid device type...\" → includes \"Try...\"\n\n\n- \"invalid major/minor device number...\" → NO \"Try...\"\n- \"invalid mode\" → NO \"Try...\"\n\nSo the \"Try...\" hint is only added for usage errors, not value validation errors. The device number and mode errors take different code paths—device errors come from parseArgs and get the hint added in main, while mode errors are printed directly in run without it. I need to restructure this so device number errors skip the hint the same way mode errors do.\n\nThe cleanest solution is to create an error type that distinguishes between errors that warrant the \"Try...\" hint and those that don't, so I can handle them appropriately regardless of where they originate.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":69702,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1670},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bf3d195-37dc-4716-b8df-76f355abf711","uuid":"97c75416-424f-4698-a46f-d96665bb01bb"}
